ition":{"commit_sha":"de0d5afcb1a1f4f01b8ae9f036bbdaa757102638","position":"1787365092561274001-ad493642-96e4-462b-bdfd-910e62b9ade2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"0a1e9bb4c97dc3d9aa7e62943f14141733663ee23f53cb32f6a884996cfc699b","event_uuid":"8dea7edc-f56f-497b-bedb-be2df44b3206","position":{"commit_sha":"476b00990df479330754d7500fe1d4c0189f32d4","position":"1787366090149179727-8dea7edc-f56f-497b-bedb-be2df44b3206"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"cbddebd3d54d1a5bc739130a14ab65c830758cb1898c9572f2df270a028a758c","event_uuid":"aa5ca037-33d1-4429-ab86-911244e66828","position":{"commit_sha":"4fed67c243719e36d497d73ef2230d1fa67f533f","position":"1787366707038434001-aa5ca037-33d1-4429-ab86-911244e66828"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"1b4576302acc143a981668c51cc7ea301ec4d892303b4ef1887883cd5774ea8b","event_uuid":"1205f030-875c-4bc5-8137-f2f1df041d93","position":{"commit_sha":"78d28c0afcc7004d1c285be09211404604f380dc","position":"1787367343380337001-1205f030-875c-4bc5-8137-f2f1df041d93"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"e421d8525454f9112888d2910270fecdb15713c813b0d3473d4ec82310785cb5","event_uuid":"315d1e57-a76e-4253-8725-bfda190fbf67","position":{"commit_sha":"d1391fe4fffe4b44c335fe6ccf3f2a75c4585e8a","position":"1787368349182456044-315d1e57-a76e-4253-8725-bfda190fbf67"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"OPERATOR RULING (recorded verbatim, attributed to the operator): \"Unreadable config should result in an error.\"\n\nThis answers this ticket's one question — do the opt-in verify.* gates keep failing OPEN on an unreadable config? — with NO, and with a posture NEITHER of the two previously argued options: an unreadable/corrupt rebar.toml must raise a loud error that fails the operation, not silently resolve gates to their defaults (fail-open), and not a fail-CLOSED gate that can only answer 'unavailable' (the measured counterfactual in steep-tired-whimbrel's decision comment — zero enforcement bought). The fault surfaces to the operator with the parse error so it gets FIXED, instead of being laundered into either a policy choice or a block nobody can act on.\n\nThis ticket therefore becomes an implementation ticket; description will be updated with the design per the plan template.","timestamp":1787334508124354001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit change 2045 review iterations: PS1 LLM-Review -1 (api-compat: undocumented public library fault-path change). PS2 documented the ConfigError raise in rebar.claim/rebar.transition docstrings, re-exported rebar.ConfigError (in __all__, pinned by test), replied that the break is the operator-ruled point. PS2 re-review still BLOCKed on 'unversioned behavior change' -> PS3 adds the CHANGELOG.md BREAKING entry and a docs/release-notes.md agent-visible contract section. Advisory (surface-parity, _mcp_errors.py): MCP surfacing deferred to ticket 8408-54bb which owns the MCP resolvers and carries the same ruling.","timestamp":1787365092561274001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Lane resumed by a new session (prior agent cancelled mid-flow; claim adopted, not re-claimed). Change 2045 PS3 (83e1d54834) inspected: LLM-Review +1, no unresolved comments. The PS1/PS2 Verified-1 votes were superseded-patchset cancellations (macOS pytest CANCELLED when the next patchset's run started), not test failures. PS3 CI run 32545864868 is in progress — all jobs green except pytest (macos-latest, py3.13) still running. Waiting for Verified +1, then Submit and close.","timestamp":1787366707038434001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"PS3 earned LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, but Gerrit Submit returned 409: server-side rebase conflicted with today's main (close-provenance enum 6e768d6f26 landed _gate_skip_expectation/gate_unreadable in close_precheck.py, plus the _plan_review_close_recheck extraction in transition_close.py). Pre-rebased locally onto origin/main (the sanctioned textual-conflict case) as PS4 (fb79a9d60e), preserving Change-Id. Resolution: _gate_skip_expectation keeps main's provenance structure but drops the UNREADABLE branch and the removed extra= kwarg (gate_enabled now raises); gate_unreadable stays in the schema/types vocabulary for historical events only — no new write produces it; main's new test_unreadable_config_records_gate_unreadable_not_gate_off asserted the pre-ruling fail-open posture and is retargeted to assert ConfigError + no close event, grounded in the recorded operator ruling. Gates locally green: 73 targeted tests pass, make lint, mypy 625 files clean, complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0. Awaiting re-votes on PS4.","timestamp":1787367343380337001}],"created_at":1787268355560489001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f5170805-5e69-4e10-b9d3-fe334ad220df","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"f5c4-b2d1-4503-4bfe"},{"link_uuid":"2f87dec4-e79b-42ca-967f-439ebd6f3f5e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"032e-6890-0e1f-4306"},{"link_uuid":"9587dfba-ed53-41a1-b037-803779e324ca","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8440-a250-a733-4870"},{"link_uuid":"8dea7edc-f56f-497b-bedb-be2df44b3206","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b445-87d2-fd39-44d9"},{"link_uuid":"315d1e57-a76e-4253-8725-bfda190fbf67","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ea9a-0df3-419f-4b09"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nOperator ruling received (see comment): **\"Unreadable config should result in an error.\"**\nThis settles the question this ticket was filed to carry — the opt-in `verify.*` gates must\nNOT keep failing OPEN on an unreadable config, and must NOT fail closed into a\nblocked-`unavailable` verdict either. An unreadable/corrupt `rebar.toml` is a FAULT the\noperator must see and fix; today `gate_enabled` (`_commands/gates.py`) swallows the\n`ConfigError` into `GateState.UNREADABLE`, prints one stderr warning, and the gated\noperation silently proceeds as if the gate were off.\n\n## Approach\n\nRaise the error at the SOURCE, so every gate consumer gets the new posture without\nper-caller re-implementation:\n\n1. `gates.gate_enabled` stops catching `ConfigError` into `GateState.UNREADABLE`. On an\n   unreadable config it raises a `ConfigError` (chained `from` the parse fault) naming the\n   gate label, the ticket, and the underlying parse error — the existing typed config-fault\n   family, so callers and tests can catch it precisely.\n2. `GateState.UNREADABLE` is removed (it becomes unreachable); `GateState` keeps\n   `ENABLED`/`DISABLED` and its `__bool__` so the ~15 test modules that monkeypatch\n   `gate_enabled` with a plain bool keep working. The `unreadable` skip verdict branch in\n   `close_plan_review_gate_check` is removed (dead); the `gate_ran` stamp and predicate\n   stay (still distinguish the `disabled` skip from a gate that ran).\n3. The `extra` parameter of `gate_enabled` (a warning-suffix clause) is dropped with the\n   warning it decorated; both call sites passing it are updated.\n4. CLI surfacing: `_cli/__init__.py main()` gains an `except ConfigError` boundary\n   (alongside `RemovedInputError`/`TrackerRootError`) printing `Error: <msg>` to stderr\n   with exit 1, so the new error is a clean operator-facing failure, not a traceback —\n   the same rendering `main()` already gives a `ConfigError` from `-c` overrides.\n5. Docs updated to the new contract: `docs/plan-review-gate.md` (the \"unreadable config\n   fails this opt-in gate off with a warning\" paragraph), `docs/config.md` bullet 6\n   (\"Loud, not silent\"), `docs/llm-framework.md`'s matching sentence.\n\n### Caller sweep (every `gate_enabled` consumer, per c504977aef's RCA)\n\n- `gates.close_plan_review_gate_check` (plan-review close gate) — PROPAGATES. Called\n  pre-lock by `transition_close`, so the error is raised BEFORE `txn.transition_core`\n  takes the write lock; the b8841ae695 property (an unreadable config does no work under\n  the lock) is preserved and stays tested. The in-lock recheck closure is only installed\n  after a pre-lock check that RAN. Precision on the rare pre-lock→lock window (the config\n  turns unreadable AFTER a passing pre-lock check): the locked recheck's `ConfigError` is\n  re-typed by `transition_core`'s fail-closed boundary (`txn.py`: `except Exception →\n  CommandError(f\"Error: {exc}\", returncode=1) from None`), so THAT path aborts loudly as\n  a `CommandError` carrying the parse-fault text in its message — exit 1, close refused —\n  but NOT as the typed, chained `ConfigError` and NOT via the CLI `ConfigError` boundary.\n  That is deliberate: `transition_core`'s re-wrap is its existing fail-closed contract\n  for the write path and is out of scope here; the typed, chained `ConfigError`\n  guarantee (AC1/AC2) applies to the pre-lock and claim paths, which are the paths an\n  unreadable-at-operation-start config actually takes.\n- `gates._plan_review_gate_applies` → `plan_review_precheck` (claim + `transition open\n  in_progress`) and `claim.py` stage-1 `--review` sensing — PROPAGATES: starting work on\n  an unreadable config fails loudly.\n- `close_precheck._completion_precheck` (completion close gate) — PROPAGATES: the close\n  fails loudly before any billable verifier work.\n- `gates.description_cap_warning` — DELIBERATE CATCH, kept: its `except Exception →\n  None` guards an advisory-only notice emitted after a write has already committed\n  (documented in its docstring and pinned by\n  `test_description_cap_warning.py::test_an_unreadable_cap_never_disturbs_the_write`).\n  The ruling scopes the error to gate resolution of gated operations; the completed\n  write must not be disturbed, and the actual claim of that ticket still errors.\n\nRead-only ops (`list`, `show`, `search`) do not resolve gates and are unaffected — the\nerror is scoped to gate resolution, exactly as the ruling demands.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_commands/gates.py` — the raise, `GateState` narrowing, docstrings.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py` — call-site signature + comment.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py` — comment describing the recheck-install\n  condition (behavioural text references the retired unreadable skip).\n- `src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py` — the `ConfigError` boundary in `main()`.\n- `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, `docs/config.md`, `docs/llm-framework.md` — contract text.\n- Tests: rewrite `tests/unit/test_gate_state_tristate_f5c4.py`,\n  `tests/unit/test_close_gate_ran_predicate_2091.py` (unreadable arm),\n  `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_gate_unreadable_config_2091.py`; new RED module\n  `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_gate_unreadable_config_errors_39f8.py`.\n\n## Testing\n\nRED before GREEN (the new module fails on current main, passes after):\n\n- Happy/failure pair at the function: readable-on → `ENABLED`, readable-off →\n  `DISABLED`; malformed `rebar.toml` → `ConfigError` raised, message names the gate\n  label, the ticket id, and the parse fault.\n- End-to-end failure paths: with a malformed `rebar.toml`, (a) `rebar.claim` fails\n  loudly naming the config fault and the ticket stays `open`; (b) a close via\n  `rebar.transition(in_progress→closed)` fails loudly BEFORE the write lock (the ticket\n  stays `in_progress`, no status event is appended, and the in-lock recheck is never\n  invoked — the b8841ae695 no-work-under-the-lock property, retargeted from \"silently\n  proceeds\" to \"errors first\").\n- Invariance guards: `disabled` skip verdict, `gate_ran` stamp semantics, and bool\n  monkeypatch compatibility unchanged.\n- Full gates: `make lint`, targeted pytest for the modules above, `make typecheck`,\n  complexity ratchet.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] With a malformed `rebar.toml`, `gate_enabled` raises `ConfigError` (chained from\n  the parse fault, message naming gate + ticket + fault) instead of returning a state —\n  checked by `tests/unit/test_gate_state_tristate_f5c4.py`.\n- [ ] With a malformed `rebar.toml`, a claim fails loudly with that error (exit ≠ 0 on\n  the CLI, typed raise in the library) leaving the ticket `open` — checked by\n  `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_gate_unreadable_config_errors_39f8.py`.\n- [ ] With a malformed `rebar.toml`, a close fails loudly with that error leaving the\n  ticket `in_progress` — checked by the same new test module.\n- [ ] The close-path error is raised BEFORE the write lock; no config read or gate work\n  happens under the lock on the unreadable path — checked by the rewritten\n  `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_gate_unreadable_config_2091.py`.\n- [ ] A readable config's behaviour is byte-identical (`ENABLED`/`DISABLED` resolution,\n  the `disabled` skip verdict, the `gate_ran` stamp, bool monkeypatch compatibility) —\n  checked by the existing gate test suites staying green.\n- [ ] `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, `docs/config.md`, and `docs/llm-framework.md` state\n  the new contract (unreadable config ⇒ error; never a silent skip, never a fake\n  `disabled`) — checked by reading the three updated sections.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/gates.py","reason":"raise ConfigError on unreadable config; remove GateState.UNREADABLE"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py","reason":"call-site signature update (extra param dropped)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py","reason":"recheck-install comment retargeted to the error posture"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py","reason":"ConfigError boundary in main() for clean operator-facing surfacing"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"replace the fail-open contract paragraph with the error contract"},{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"update bullet 6 Loud-not-silent gate posture"},{"path":"docs/llm-framework.md","reason":"update the unreadable-config sentence"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gate_state_tristate_f5c4.py","reason":"retarget tristate assertions to the raise"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_close_gate_ran_predicate_2091.py","reason":"unreadable arm now expects a raise"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_gate_unreadable_config_2091.py","reason":"close now errors before the lock instead of proceeding"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_completion_gate.py","reason":"old fail-open pinning test retargeted to the error contract"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_gate_unreadable_config_errors_39f8.py","reason":"new RED-first end-to-end error-posture tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","032e-6890-0e1f-4306"],["relates_to","8440-a250-a733-4870"],["relates_to","b445-87d2-fd39-44d9"],["relates_to","ea9a-0df3-419f-4b09"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"1204a70c-f972-4472-b452-29ad7de051e4","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"39f8-ae7c-f651-4333","ticket_type":"task","title":"Operator ruling: should the opt-in verify.* gates keep failing OPEN on an unreadable config?","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6b375682-aec1-4cc5-8c5f-ba6a07151249","77581146-f10d-4c08-8b2a-a209e39af033","21fcbfad-569e-478d-a9f2-8e3560eaa50b","a20a4b5e-409d-4025-8d10-007b63701f91","71d2067e-af13-47c3-af97-b5654a418a2e","1204a70c-f972-4472-b452-29ad7de051e4","129b507c-420e-4f46-8ff6-fb601b28de76","2e46f890-1f37-415e-84e5-608a88d2621d","2f87dec4-e79b-42ca-967f-439ebd6f3f5e","9587dfba-ed53-41a1-b037-803779e324ca","ad493642-96e4-462b-bdfd-910e62b9ade2","8dea7edc-f56f-497b-bedb-be2df44b3206","aa5ca037-33d1-4429-ab86-911244e66828","1205f030-875c-4bc5-8137-f2f1df041d93","315d1e57-a76e-4253-8725-bfda190fbf67"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787368349182456045,"uuid":"92b74a82-603a-4673-93f9-1a0b84b63fa8"}